  "title": "Gemini became a more capable default",
  "summary": "A week of making generations more predictable: better model routing, media inputs, account controls, and fewer requests doing the same work twice.\n\n`gemini` and `gemini-search` moved to Gemini 3 Flash Preview, while `gemini-fast` offers Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite. Gemini gained video input in chat completions, and fixes across the week made default tools, cached-token usage, and model routing work more reliably.\n\nZ-Image now carries the requested aspect ratio through generation and upscaling, with face-aware restoration when faces are detected. Seedance Pro passes along video aspect ratios, Seedream 4.5 Pro uses requested seeds, and Veo image-to-video uses the supplied image as its first frame. The image API also handles unencoded reference URLs more gracefully.\n\nUsage records are available as paginated JSON or CSV, with a dashboard download and recent Pollen spend beside the balance. API keys can be limited to selected models, and Enter now shows when keys were last used and when they expire. New accounts are assigned the SPORE subscription automatically.\n\nChat completions gained a `repetition_penalty` control, and `openai-audio` accepts all 13 listed voices. Temperature handling now follows the resolved model, avoiding unsupported-temperature errors even when a request uses an alias.",
